   ],
   "rule": null,
   "text": "Most words come from a **three-consonant root** poured into patterns. Knowing a root helps you guess new words: d-r-s (study) → **درس** (lesson), **مدرسة** (school), **مدرّس** (teacher), **دراسة** (studies). Dictionaries often list verbs by their basic form and derived forms II–X.",
